# apply_tma2_decay_roll.py — fence TMA2_DECAY_ROLL_20261016   (requires TMA2_SL_CLOSE_CONFIRM_20261016)
#
# TMA_V2 BACKTEST ONLY — decay roll. Absent (or enabled: false) = the sealed
# run byte-for-byte (proven against the runner's .bak in the suite).
#
#   s1.roll = {at_pct, sl_pct, max}
#     When the SOLD leg's premium falls to at_pct % of its entry premium
#     (touch, gap → open — exactly like the TP), the spread closes (exit
#     reason ROLL) and a fresh spread is sold on the next candle: same sold
#     side and expiry, highest premium under the main cap (a different
#     strike), new hedge from the hedge rules, same lots as the parent.
#     The new leg (cond E1R1 / E2R1 …) keeps the trend's crossover exit and
#     the main TP, with its OWN stop: sl_pct % above its entry (0 = no stop).
#     It may roll again until `max` rolls for that original position.
#     No roll on the contract's expiry day, none whose new entry would fall
#     outside the entry session window, none when no strike/hedge is
#     available — in those cases the touch is ignored for the rest of that
#     day and the position runs on with its real TP (it can roll next
#     session). SELL + POSITIONAL only; refused with partial booking, a
#     close-basis SL or the EOD MTM cut.
#   DIAG: decay_roll, rolls, roll_skipped_window, roll_skipped_select.
#
# History: the 2026-09-21 continuation experiment rolled at 33% (DECAY 0.33)
# with the normal 12% stop: +₹0.28L, judged noise, reverted. This run tests
# the two untried corners: a deeper decay (25 / 20) and a wide or no stop
# on the new leg.
#
# Pre-registered (sealed config otherwise): at_pct {25, 20} × rolled SL
# {none, 50%}, max 1 (4 runs) + the best of those at max 2 (1 run).
# Pass bar: scoreboard order, both halves better, net ex-top-20 not worse,
# rolled legs net-positive on their own in BOTH halves, and the winner's
# neighbour also beating sealed.
